    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d64">

                <pb facs="0063" n="53" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg53"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/1–1749: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-17">January 17,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received January 17—2:41 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>140. Initial Shanghai reaction to Communist peace terms as reported <hi
                        rendition="#italic">China Press</hi> January 16, Pan Kung-chan, Chairman
                    City Council, states CCP terms better than no response at all and calls <pb
                        facs="0064" n="54" xml:id="pg54"/> for immediate 2 months’ cease-fire with
                    both sides sending delegates Nanking and Shanghai for peace talks.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 140; repeated Nanking 110.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
